            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• Margins are profit as a % of the row's revenue, from the top of the P&L down: Gross (after the direct cost of the product or service), Contribution (after selling and delivery costs), Adj. EBITDA (after running costs such as marketing, R&D and admin), Operating (after depreciation and one-off items).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#101b2b"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• Read across a row: each margin is lower than the one before, because more costs are taken off.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#101b2b"
                    }
